---
source: sched/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: "help_output(\"chrt\")"
---
Manipulate the real-time attributes of a process

Usage: chrt [options] <priority> <command> [<arg>...]
       chrt [options] --pid [-p] <priority> <pid>
       chrt [options] --pid [-p] <pid>

Arguments:
  [ARGS]...  Positional arguments: priority and/or PID/command

Options:
  -p, --pid                              Operate on an existing PID
  -m, --max                              Show min/max valid priorities, then exit
  -v, --verbose                          Show status information
  -R, --reset-on-fork                    Set SCHED_RESET_ON_FORK flag
  -a, --all-tasks                        Operate on all tasks (threads) of a given PID
  -o, --other                            Set scheduling policy to SCHED_OTHER
  -f, --fifo                             Set scheduling policy to SCHED_FIFO
  -r, --rr                               Set scheduling policy to SCHED_RR
  -b, --batch                            Set scheduling policy to SCHED_BATCH
  -i, --idle                             Set scheduling policy to SCHED_IDLE
  -d, --deadline                         Set scheduling policy to SCHED_DEADLINE
  -T, --sched-runtime <SCHED_RUNTIME>    Runtime parameter for SCHED_DEADLINE (nanoseconds)
  -P, --sched-period <SCHED_PERIOD>      Period parameter for SCHED_DEADLINE (nanoseconds)
  -D, --sched-deadline <SCHED_DEADLINE>  Deadline parameter for SCHED_DEADLINE (nanoseconds)
  -h, --help                             Print help
